# Plural and number formatting
@scenario tutorial_lesson_47
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/47_plural_format.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt formatted]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: The same dialogue will display a different plural form when the number changes.
@label lab
> Set count to zero -> zero
> Set count to one -> one
> Set count to three -> three
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Practice exercise -> practice
> Review question -> check
@label zero
[set lab_books 0]
[jump result]
@label one
[set lab_books 1]
[jump result]
@label three
[set lab_books 3]
@label result
# region formatted
ginger: {lab_books, plural, =0{No notebooks} one{# notebook} other{# notebooks}} on the desk.
# endregion
[jump lab]
@label return_hub
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_47]
[flag tutorial_done_47]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_10]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Change the count to three. What do you expect?
> The literal # symbol. -> practice_hint
> Three notebooks. -> practice_result
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: The explicit match takes precedence before the plural category fallback.
[jump practice]
@label practice_result
ginger: The explicit match takes precedence before the plural category fallback.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the lab again -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Which plural form applies at count 0?
> The explicit =0 branch. -> correct
> The one branch. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
ginger: The explicit match takes precedence before the plural category fallback.
[jump check]
@label correct
ginger: The explicit match takes precedence before the plural category fallback.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
